# The example scripts and the stamps of their thumbnails are hashed
# (`cargo xtask example-thumbs`, xtask/src/thumbs.rs): LF in every
# checkout, also with core.autocrlf on Windows.
docs/examples/*.json text eol=lf
docs/examples/thumbs/STAMPS.txt text eol=lf
# Files tests read byte for byte, and files the packages carry as they are
# (a desktop entry, a shell script and AppRun must keep LF on Linux and
# macOS even when they were checked out on Windows): LF in every checkout.
# On Windows with core.autocrlf the golden STEP text and the desktop entry
# came out with CRLF, and their tests failed (CI, 2026-10-30).
crates/*/tests/golden/** text eol=lf
packaging/** text eol=lf
*.step text eol=lf
# Binary files last, so no text rule above (packaging/**) claims them:
# a later line wins in .gitattributes.
*.png binary
*.hdr binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.3dcraft binary
*.3dcraftjig binary
*.3dcraftasm binary
